# Architecture Decision Records (ADRs)

Canonical how-to: [`docs/adr/README.md`](../../docs/adr/README.md). Files live under `docs/adr/` as `NNNN-short-slug.md`.

## When an ADR is required

Write or update an ADR in the **same PR** (or planning handoff that lands with the PR) when you:

- Implement a Cursor **plan** that locks product/architecture shape
- **Discuss and lock** a decision with the user (plugin boundaries, planes, identity, lifecycle, “we will not do X”)
- Change an existing locked decision so older ADRs would mislead future work

```
✅ New connection type / provider registry; provenance keyed by id; Nest factory
✅ Explicit non-goals (e.g. no background git sync; no auto-delete cache on remove)
❌ Pure bugfix, copy tweak, or formatting-only PR
❌ Restating operator how-to that already belongs only in docs/*.md
```

## How to write

1. Next free `NNNN` - never renumber after merge
2. Nygard fields: Status, Date, Context, Decision, Consequences; Alternatives when useful
3. Status `Accepted` when the implementing PR merges (or in that PR)
4. Link related issues and code paths; link operator how-to under `docs/` instead of duplicating it
5. Update the **index table** in `docs/adr/README.md`

## Superseding

When a new decision replaces an old one:

1. Add the new ADR (`Accepted`)
2. Set the old ADR Status to **`Superseded`** and link the successor
3. Leave the old file in place (history); do not delete or renumber
4. Fix stale “remains #…” or “we chose X” claims in `docs/` that the successor invalidates

```
✅ ADR-0009 Accepted for clone cache; later ADR-0010 Accepted for forge; 0009 notes dual-run / what forge does not replace yet
✅ Old ADR Status: Superseded by ADR-00NN (link)

❌ Quietly contradict an Accepted ADR in code with no record
❌ Edit history by deleting or renumbering ADRs
```

## Plans and issues

Locked bullets in a plan or GitHub issue comment are not enough by themselves - promote them into an ADR when implementation starts (or in the PR that ships them). Follow-on issues may defer schema/UX detail, but the **decision** still gets an ADR when it lands.
